{number: 116}
{title: The God of Abraham Praise}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [G] God of Abraham [D] praise, who [G] reigns enthroned a-[D] bove;
Ancient of [G] everlasting days, and [C] God of [G] [D7] [G] love.
Jehovah, great I AM! by [D] earth and heav'n con-[G] fest;
I bow and [C] bless the [G] sacred Name, for-[D7] ever [G] blest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [G] God of Abraham [D] praise, at [G] whose supreme com-[D] mand
From earth I [G] rise, and seek the joys at [C] His right [G] [D7] [G] hand:
I all on earth forsake, its [D] wisdom, fame, and [G] pow'r;
And Him my [C] only [G] portion make, my [D7] shield and [G] tow'r.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [G] by Himself hath [D] sworn, I [G] on His oath de-[D] pend,
I shall, on [G] eagle wings upborne, to [C] heav'n a-[G] [D7] [G] scend:
I shall behold His face, I [D] shall His pow'r a-[G] dore,
And sing the [C] wonders [G] of His grace for-[D7] ever-[G] more.
{end_of_verse}
